---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, correctionUrl } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About and contribute" description="What PQC Deps is, who runs it, and how to contribute library data.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A free, open catalog that answers one question for developers and security teams: which of my
      dependencies are quantum-vulnerable, and what do I upgrade to?
    </p>
    <p>
      Governments and regulators are setting deadlines for migrating to post-quantum cryptography.
      The facts about which libraries support it are scattered across changelogs, issue trackers,
      mailing lists and blog posts. {SITE.name} collects them in one place, with a source for every
      claim.
    </p>
    <p>
      We focus on <strong>open-source libraries and packages</strong>, not vendor products, and on
      checking your project's dependency files.
    </p>

    <h2>Contribute</h2>
    <p>Each library is a YAML file in the <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub repository</a>.</p>
    <h3>Report a mistake</h3>
    <p>
      Use the <em>Suggest a correction</em> link on any library page, or
      <a href={correctionUrl()}>open a correction issue</a>. Please include a link to the source.
    </p>
    <h3>Request a library</h3>
    <p>
      The easiest way: fill in the <a href="/request">request form</a>. A maintainer reviews it, and
      the evidence is gathered automatically.
    </p>
    <h3>Add or update a library yourself</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Copy an existing file in <code>data/libraries/</code>. The file name must match its <code>id</code>.</li>
      <li>
        For every claim, add a source with the URL, a verbatim <code>quote</code> from that page, and
        the date you read it. If you can't cite it, leave it <code>unknown</code>.
      </li>
      <li>Run <code>npm run validate</code> locally.</li>
      <li>Open a pull request. A maintainer checks the sources before merging.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Maintainers of a listed library are especially welcome to correct their entry. A link to your
      release notes or docs is all we need.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      The data is licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>: reuse
      it freely with attribution. The code is MIT.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
